ymfm: the licence file beside the code, as libADLMIDI has it

ymfm is under the BSD 3-Clause licence, whose second condition asks that a redistribution in binary form reproduce the copyright notice, the conditions and the disclaimer in the documentation or other materials that come with it. libADLMIDI keeps ymfm's LICENSE beside its copy of ymfm, in src/chips/ymfm/; here the notice stands only at the top of each of the thirteen ymfm source files. A program that gathers the licence files found beside the code a binary was built from, as ADLplug-Next's packaging does, therefore finds libOPNMIDI's own licences for ymfm and not ymfm's, and the binary goes out without the notice that the second condition asks for.

This adds that file, byte for byte the one libADLMIDI carries (blob f73e841). Its 29 lines are, word for word, the notice, the conditions and the disclaimer that the header of every ymfm file here holds, so the licence of the code does not change; the notice now also stands beside it, where such programs, and people, look for it.

This is ADLplug-Next's own patch, applied to the submodule by cmake/Patches.cmake when CMake configures, and it goes away once the change is upstream.

diff --git a/src/chips/ymfm/LICENSE b/src/chips/ymfm/LICENSE
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..f73e841
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/chips/ymfm/LICENSE
@@ -0,0 +1,29 @@
